WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.099 --> 00:00:03.779
So I sit on yesterday's bonus show that today
I was going to go through this new middle

00:00:03.779 --> 00:00:06.431
East peace plan that has been released by
Donald [inaudible]

00:00:06.431 --> 00:00:09.370
Trump and by Israeli prime minister Benjamin
Netanyahu.

00:00:09.370 --> 00:00:10.370
So let's do that.

00:00:10.370 --> 00:00:12.750
But in order to do it, we have to establish
a few things.

00:00:12.750 --> 00:00:17.130
First, number one, Donald Trump knows nothing
about the Israeli Palestinian conflict.

00:00:17.130 --> 00:00:21.230
He's self congratulating by calling this the
deal of the century.

00:00:21.230 --> 00:00:25.070
He thought Jared Cushner was going to achieve
middle Eastern peace.

00:00:25.070 --> 00:00:28.550
It's a total joke at the get go and Trump
has completely in over his head.

00:00:28.550 --> 00:00:34.399
Number two, this entire thing is absurd at
its face because you have impeached president

00:00:34.399 --> 00:00:39.179
Donald Trump and indicted prime minister Benjamin
Netanyahu is saying, Hey, we figured out a

00:00:39.179 --> 00:00:44.170
great plan with no Palestinian involvement
in actually figuring out this plan.

00:00:44.170 --> 00:00:45.339
So that's ridiculous.

00:00:45.339 --> 00:00:50.269
And the number three, this is very clearly
time to suppress coverage of both Donald Trump's

00:00:50.269 --> 00:00:54.850
impeachment and Benjamin Netanyahu is indictment
respectively.

00:00:54.850 --> 00:00:58.929
It's laughable at its face, but let's take
a little bit of a look at the parameters to

00:00:58.929 --> 00:01:04.850
see if we by chance come across something
in this quote deal that makes sense.

00:01:04.850 --> 00:01:09.729
Palestinian leaders have rejected the deal
on principle because it includes some annexations

00:01:09.729 --> 00:01:11.500
of West bank land.

00:01:11.500 --> 00:01:17.390
Now I've said before, I'm 100% against settlements
by Israel, which violate international law.

00:01:17.390 --> 00:01:22.210
The settlements need to stop, they need to
stop now and in any realistic longterm peace

00:01:22.210 --> 00:01:25.530
deal, and I'll lay out what that looks like
a little bit later.

00:01:25.530 --> 00:01:31.990
There is going to be some West bank land on
which there are settlements likely swapped

00:01:31.990 --> 00:01:38.390
for land of equivalent value, uh, from Israel
for a Palestinian state.

00:01:38.390 --> 00:01:44.229
Arafat in the 90s said that it's potentially
okay if the land is equivalent, whatever that

00:01:44.229 --> 00:01:45.229
means.

00:01:45.229 --> 00:01:49.320
That's going to have to be debated, but this
nothing is going to happen if there cannot

00:01:49.320 --> 00:01:51.460
be some land swaps.

00:01:51.460 --> 00:01:56.960
The deal that Donald Trump and Benjamin Netanyahu
have put forth would include a four year freeze

00:01:56.960 --> 00:01:59.109
on new settlement construction.

00:01:59.109 --> 00:02:00.109
That's a start.

00:02:00.109 --> 00:02:05.899
The problem with it is that does that mean
that an existing settlement cannot expand

00:02:05.899 --> 00:02:11.040
or that simply there can be no new settlements
and that difference is actually a really significant

00:02:11.040 --> 00:02:12.040
one.

00:02:12.040 --> 00:02:18.800
It will also provide a path to Palestinians
for a contiguous territory for a future Palestinian

00:02:18.800 --> 00:02:21.300
state when certain conditions of statehood
are met.

00:02:21.300 --> 00:02:25.260
Now of course Palestinians are not going to
agree to the conditions that are outlined.

00:02:25.260 --> 00:02:30.220
The contiguity of the state is an important
thing and from the maps that have been put

00:02:30.220 --> 00:02:36.220
out, it looks like Gaza and the West bank
and a capital in East Jerusalem would be contiguous,

00:02:36.220 --> 00:02:40.000
uh, based on, on roads that would be made
part of the state.

00:02:40.000 --> 00:02:47.190
So in principle impeached Trump and indicted
Netanyahu establishing this without Palestinian

00:02:47.190 --> 00:02:49.070
involvement is a joke.

00:02:49.070 --> 00:02:55.520
Palestinian, uh, a Palestinian capital in
East Jerusalem is included in this, which

00:02:55.520 --> 00:03:00.770
is good, but it's mentioned only as part of
East Jerusalem.

00:03:00.770 --> 00:03:05.330
That's going to be a tough negotiating point
as well if there is ever a negotiation to

00:03:05.330 --> 00:03:06.330
happen.

00:03:06.330 --> 00:03:10.670
Um, and in total this is effectively a political
stunt.

00:03:10.670 --> 00:03:12.150
That's all that this is.

00:03:12.150 --> 00:03:16.270
And because this has come up and it's an opportunity
to do it.

00:03:16.270 --> 00:03:18.350
Let me review my peace plan.

00:03:18.350 --> 00:03:23.950
And as I said last time I did this years ago,
almost everyone is going to find something

00:03:23.950 --> 00:03:29.020
they don't like about what I believe and eventual
plan would look like.

00:03:29.020 --> 00:03:32.730
Every good compromise leaves everyone at least
a little bit upset.

00:03:32.730 --> 00:03:34.270
That's why it's called compromise.

00:03:34.270 --> 00:03:38.010
But this is the way I would see the most likely
path forward.

00:03:38.010 --> 00:03:42.020
First of all, we have to talk about who's
in charge of negotiations.

00:03:42.020 --> 00:03:46.720
Benjamin Netanyahu is not going to preside
over serious Israeli Palestinian peace.

00:03:46.720 --> 00:03:48.120
It's just not going to happen.

00:03:48.120 --> 00:03:49.870
He's shown that it is not in his interest.

00:03:49.870 --> 00:03:51.360
It is not in his interests.

00:03:51.360 --> 00:03:57.780
He benefits from more attention and uh, and
not having any kind of serious prospect for

00:03:57.780 --> 00:03:58.780
peace.

00:03:58.780 --> 00:04:02.050
So Benjamin Netanyahu cannot be the Israeli
prime minister.

00:04:02.050 --> 00:04:07.190
If we are going to see serious opportunities
for peace, Hamas must be replaced by a more

00:04:07.190 --> 00:04:10.650
secular Palestinian authority in Gaza right
away.

00:04:10.650 --> 00:04:14.780
Hamas is not going to be a serious negotiator
of peace.

00:04:14.780 --> 00:04:17.370
What would mock muda boss's role be?

00:04:17.370 --> 00:04:19.930
They're currently in charge of the West bank.

00:04:19.930 --> 00:04:21.920
I'm open to expanding the role of MOC.

00:04:21.920 --> 00:04:24.620
Buddha boss Hamas does not want that.

00:04:24.620 --> 00:04:28.500
Hamas has actually assassinated photog members
in recent years.

00:04:28.500 --> 00:04:35.310
A boss, uh, has, has often, um, uh, given,
you know, lie riddled speeches at the United

00:04:35.310 --> 00:04:41.390
nations, but to the extent that a boss might
be a productive partner, that's what I care

00:04:41.390 --> 00:04:42.390
about.

00:04:42.390 --> 00:04:48.210
I'm open to a boss being involved in the eventual
secular, ideally Palestinian authority that

00:04:48.210 --> 00:04:49.660
would be in charge.

00:04:49.660 --> 00:04:53.690
Law of return for Jews to Israel is going
to have to be maintained.

00:04:53.690 --> 00:04:56.250
I don't see how you put a deal together without
it.

00:04:56.250 --> 00:05:01.980
Um, the, the, the whole point of Israel is
Jews have been and continue to be discriminated

00:05:01.980 --> 00:05:04.970
against and kicked out of so many parts of
the world.

00:05:04.970 --> 00:05:08.030
Israel is a place Jews know they can go period.

00:05:08.030 --> 00:05:14.800
And as long as that is maintained, um, I don't
know that I care too much about whether Israel

00:05:14.800 --> 00:05:17.100
is called a Jewish state.

00:05:17.100 --> 00:05:22.860
This is a point of contention that I am sort
of flexible on as long as the law of return

00:05:22.860 --> 00:05:23.860
remains.

00:05:23.860 --> 00:05:25.930
Uh, that, that is what I think is important.

00:05:25.930 --> 00:05:32.240
The Palestinian law of return for Palestinians
to return to Israel is going to have to be

00:05:32.240 --> 00:05:33.670
conceded to some degree.

00:05:33.670 --> 00:05:38.250
And this is something that certainly governments
like the Netanyahu government have not wanted.

00:05:38.250 --> 00:05:40.490
It can't be for 5 million Palestinians.

00:05:40.490 --> 00:05:41.560
It's just not going to happen.

00:05:41.560 --> 00:05:45.700
So again, I know that a lot of the reaction
to this will be, David, you're acting like

00:05:45.700 --> 00:05:48.900
this wouldn't be fair or that wouldn't be
fair.

00:05:48.900 --> 00:05:54.310
I'm trying to get to what is each side likely
going to have to concede to have a serious

00:05:54.310 --> 00:06:00.450
opportunity and the Israel is not going to
concede return for 5 million Palestinians,

00:06:00.450 --> 00:06:05.310
but some reasonable number that makes sense,
uh, should be included.

00:06:05.310 --> 00:06:09.420
Once the blockade on Gaza is released, which
it should be, anyone who wants to move back

00:06:09.420 --> 00:06:12.669
to Gaza or the West bank should be free to
do so.

00:06:12.669 --> 00:06:17.250
And at that point it will be up to the Palestinian
authority to decide how many people will they

00:06:17.250 --> 00:06:21.010
allow to move into Gaza and the West bank
and East Jerusalem.

00:06:21.010 --> 00:06:26.950
Um, in the past a hood, Barack, for example,
suggested a symbolic number of Palestinian

00:06:26.950 --> 00:06:30.760
returners and otherwise significant financial
reparations.

00:06:30.760 --> 00:06:35.620
And I think that something like that would,
would likely be what has to happen.

00:06:35.620 --> 00:06:37.950
Importantly, what are the borders, right?

00:06:37.950 --> 00:06:39.990
This is a big point of contention.

00:06:39.990 --> 00:06:44.980
I believe that the borders are going to have
to be more or less the proposed Clinton borders

00:06:44.980 --> 00:06:46.830
from the 1990s.

00:06:46.830 --> 00:06:50.139
And that's very similar to a lot of the recent
ideas that have been put forward.

00:06:50.139 --> 00:06:54.530
The Palestinian territory will include the
West bank and Gaza and East Jerusalem.

00:06:54.530 --> 00:06:59.889
Um, the problem is that the limits of East
Jerusalem are disputed.

00:06:59.889 --> 00:07:02.949
That's when Donald Trump says part of East
Jerusalem.

00:07:02.949 --> 00:07:05.410
This conflict is what he's getting at.

00:07:05.410 --> 00:07:09.540
Let's imagine that there could be an agreement
as to what the lines of East Jerusalem would

00:07:09.540 --> 00:07:10.540
be.

00:07:10.540 --> 00:07:16.790
Jerusalem, um, uh, would Easter reus alum
at whatever agreed upon borders would be decided

00:07:16.790 --> 00:07:18.720
there plus Gaza, the West bank.

00:07:18.720 --> 00:07:22.890
And again, something linking them to make
it a contiguous state.

00:07:22.890 --> 00:07:27.720
Uh, Jerusalem becoming the capital of Israel
for international purposes.

00:07:27.720 --> 00:07:31.720
This is controversial, um, is in many Israelis
want this.

00:07:31.720 --> 00:07:34.690
Certainly the Netanyahu government wants it
right now internationally, the Capitol is

00:07:34.690 --> 00:07:36.560
Televiv internally.

00:07:36.560 --> 00:07:38.610
Jerusalem is sort of the Capitol.

00:07:38.610 --> 00:07:44.130
I'm fine with Jerusalem becoming the capital
of Israel for international purpose purposes,

00:07:44.130 --> 00:07:48.600
uh, and Easter Russel and becoming the Palestinian
capital.

00:07:48.600 --> 00:07:53.100
I think that there is going to have to be
some something figured out with regard to

00:07:53.100 --> 00:07:58.000
the Jewish quarter of the old city in East
Jerusalem.

00:07:58.000 --> 00:08:01.410
That's probably going to have to remain under
Israeli sovereignty.

00:08:01.410 --> 00:08:04.000
We could do an entire show just about that.

00:08:04.000 --> 00:08:09.460
But among the list of complex options, you
probably are going to have to negotiate.

00:08:09.460 --> 00:08:14.980
Um, the Jewish quarter of remaining part of
Israel, there was desecration of the Jewish

00:08:14.980 --> 00:08:18.000
quarter from 49 to 67.

00:08:18.000 --> 00:08:22.600
You can read more about that if you care to,
but that would probably be, uh, something

00:08:22.600 --> 00:08:25.449
that has to remain under Israeli control.

00:08:25.449 --> 00:08:30.800
Of course, Israel has to immediately stop
all settlement building period.

00:08:30.800 --> 00:08:35.259
Israel needs to agree in principle to remove
some settlements, they're going to have to

00:08:35.259 --> 00:08:38.269
agree to remove some settlements to get a
deal done.

00:08:38.269 --> 00:08:42.740
And then again, the larger settlements that
are not realistically speaking going to be,

00:08:42.740 --> 00:08:44.459
uh, dismantled.

00:08:44.459 --> 00:08:49.019
There will have to be land swaps and the land
swaps have to be of equivalent meaningful

00:08:49.019 --> 00:08:50.029
land.

00:08:50.029 --> 00:08:53.519
Not all the settlements at this point are
going to realistically be removed.

00:08:53.519 --> 00:08:56.230
I wish it were different, but this is the
reality.

00:08:56.230 --> 00:09:01.860
As Arafat said in the 90s, if they are meaningful
land swaps, it's conceivably something that

00:09:01.860 --> 00:09:05.509
Palestinians could be open to the security
situation.

00:09:05.509 --> 00:09:10.439
What happens with travel and checkpoints and
the Gaza blockade, the Palestinians will immediately,

00:09:10.439 --> 00:09:15.440
and this, this is why Hamas is unlikely to
be a good negotiating partner.

00:09:15.440 --> 00:09:19.110
Palestinians will have to stop all rocket
attacks immediately.

00:09:19.110 --> 00:09:21.769
All tunnel building would have to stop immediately.

00:09:21.769 --> 00:09:24.610
And existing tunnels meant to circumvent the
security.

00:09:24.610 --> 00:09:27.660
A status quo would have to be destroyed right
away.

00:09:27.660 --> 00:09:32.839
Um, there would have to be an agreement to
demilitarize Gaza as part of a peace agreement.

00:09:32.839 --> 00:09:36.529
And in the two year period after the withdrawal
is real from Gaza.

00:09:36.529 --> 00:09:41.259
Remember, but before the blockade was put
in, there were just thousands of rockets.

00:09:41.259 --> 00:09:47.860
So there must be a demilitarization and ideally
Hamas would simply not be part of these negotiations.

00:09:47.860 --> 00:09:52.610
As I, as much as I think Benjamin Netanyahu
will not be part of any credible negotiation.

00:09:52.610 --> 00:09:54.959
I don't think Hamas will be either.

00:09:54.959 --> 00:10:00.480
Israel has to remove the blockade and the
way that it would have to be done as conditional

00:10:00.480 --> 00:10:06.050
Israel will remove the blockade immediately
and as long as there is a demilitarization

00:10:06.050 --> 00:10:13.579
uh, in Gaza and no rocket launches is held
to the blockade removal would have to be held

00:10:13.579 --> 00:10:15.450
to as well as part of the agreement.

00:10:15.450 --> 00:10:18.429
And then a sort of broader key point.

00:10:18.429 --> 00:10:20.269
All claims must be renounced.

00:10:20.269 --> 00:10:25.769
In other words, both sides have to say as
part of this agreement we renounce claims

00:10:25.769 --> 00:10:28.040
and this is the end of the conflict.

00:10:28.040 --> 00:10:33.230
If in the future things are done that violate
that agreement, then they are violating an

00:10:33.230 --> 00:10:38.949
international agreement rather than one of
these nonbinding things that negotiators may

00:10:38.949 --> 00:10:39.949
put together.

00:10:39.949 --> 00:10:42.790
There has to be a, this is the end of the
conflict.

00:10:42.790 --> 00:10:44.600
We renounce all claims.

00:10:44.600 --> 00:10:46.699
This is the agreement going forward.

00:10:46.699 --> 00:10:49.480
Um, is this likely to happen anytime soon?

00:10:49.480 --> 00:10:50.610
No, it is not.

00:10:50.610 --> 00:10:51.610
And is it likely to happen under Donald Trump?

00:10:51.610 --> 00:10:51.612
Definitely not.

